; Find the next object that fits noun phrase 2 and passes the check
;
; Like #R$7CFC for the second noun phrase of a command: asks the lookup routine
; in IY (through #R$7CC9, HL = RecBuf2) for the next candidate, keeps it in
; SecondObject ($B6E9), sets bit 1 of RecWork1 ($793E) and runs the whole
; command check with #R$7AED, which needs both objects. The loop repeats while
; the check refuses (Z) and ends on the first accepted object or when the
; lookup is exhausted. Used by #R$7D17.
;
; IY Lookup routine: #R$9DD9 (objects around) or #R$9EA0 (exits), set by #R$7D17
; IX Cursor of the lookup, kept by it between calls
; O:A $FF when no candidate is left, otherwise ActionAllowed (not 0)
; O:F Z when no candidate is left
; O:SecondObject The accepted object
@label=NextNoun2Match
c$7D54 LD HL,$7948   ;
 $7D57 CALL $7CC9             ; next candidate for phrase 2
 $7D5A CP $FF                 ; $FF: none left
 $7D5C RET Z         ;
 $7D5D LD ($B6E9),A           ; SecondObject
 $7D60 LD HL,$793E   ;
 $7D63 SET 1,(HL)             ; RecWork1 bit 1: phrase 2 has a candidate
 $7D65 CALL $7AED             ; full check of the command
 $7D68 JR Z,$7D54             ; refused: try the next one
 $7D6A RET           ;
